{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDU1mVi7DaXAsxxPX6F1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed E05–E09 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. The batch validator (`--batch E05,E06,E07,E08,E09 --before-challenges`, with `--fix`) printed `Valid`: 4 gaps and 1 na_candidate, no injection attempts. I didn't run challenges, and I didn't run the repository code. I used the specified interpreter throughout.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reasons |\n|---|---|---|\n| E05 | gap | Tools are keyed by bare name (`app/mcp_client.py:100`). Duplicate names overwrite silently (`app/tools/__init__.py:66`). Approvals match on tool name only (`app/approvals.py:76`). `refresh_tools` skips the pin check. |\n| E06 | gap | `erp_call` allows operations by name prefix (`app/gate.py:35`). The `vendor.` and `invoice.` prefixes admit `vendor.update_remit_to`, `invoice.mark_paid` and `invoice.void` without approval. The token cache is keyed by audience, scope and tenant, not by delegated subject (`app/identity.py:95`). |\n| E07 | na_candidate | I found no peer-agent endpoint, so all five checks are `unknown`. The inbound routes are `/runs`, `/slack/interactions`, `/ingest/mail` and `/healthz`. This needs a fresh challenge before governance can accept it. |\n| E08 | gap | The extractor sub-agent asks for the role `line_item_extractor`, but `config/tools.yaml` defines `extractor`. The lookup falls back to the full procurement tool set (`app/tools/__init__.py:69`), which includes `pay_invoice`. The child also reuses the parent's cached token (`app/identity.py:95`). |\n| E09 | gap | The halt flag is read only at run start (`app/loop.py:127`). The model loop, extractor loop and child spawn never re-check it. Nothing is cancelled, no tokens are revoked, and no completed outside effects are recorded on stop. |\n\n- **Unknown checks:** E06.1, E06.4, E06.6 and E06.7 are `unknown`, and so are E08.2 and E08.3. The evidence for those lives outside this repo (the gateway, the STS, downstream services), or I found no fail-open branch but couldn't confirm the rest.\n- **Shared evidence:** `app/identity.py:95` backs both E06 and E08, so each lists the other in `also_affects`.\n- **Prescan hits:** I confirmed H001 (the prefix match) under E06. I dismissed H002, H005, H006 and H007 with reasons. I left H003 and H004 unresolved because they belong to B11, outside this batch.\n- **Findings file:** I added evidence entries for E07 and E05, and filled in `scope` and `repo`. I did this with a small JSON edit, because `answer.py` has no option for item-level evidence.\n- **Not run:** no `yes` answers, so no coverage ledgers were needed. I didn't write `brace-findings.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":984,"cache_read_input_tokens":86919,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":984},"output_tokens":816,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"440aace4-3591-46d8-9721-cf8df38e93d3","uuid":"95a12390-88c8-46b8-a757-5a4364d5d962","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:11:23.445Z","request_id":"req_011CgDU1m98Txa4CKR5mWbty"}
